  "query_preview": "..Weather for the long term continues to look unsettled as \nforecast guidance continues to show multiple lows moving into the \npanhandle for the end of the week and into the weekend. Forecast \nguidance still shows some uncertainty with the exact location and \nstrength of the low moving in for Thursday. This low will track \naround the parent low which looks to remain near Kodiak Island. \nWhile the parent low remains in the Western Gulf, some forecast \nguidance is pointing towards a low forming on the triple point \nconvergence for Friday which could bring another shot of moisture \nand winds to the panhandle. \n\nAttention then turns towards the weekend as deterministic and \nensemble forecast guidance have the remnants of Typhoon Koguma \nmoving into the Gulf and interacting with the low that has been \nlingering in the area. Right now, guidance is split on whether this \nsystem that develops moves north into the southern panhandle or \ndives south. Right now, Euro/EPS guidance wants to bring the low \nnorth along Haida Gwaii Sunday evening into Monday morning before \nmoving into the Southern Panhandle. The GFS/GEFS wants to bring the \nstrengthening low up to Haida Gwaii before diving south in British \nColumbia and the PNW. Canadian/GEPS is leaning more towards the Euro \nsolution but not as strong and does not move the low as far north. \nDue to the uncertainty of this track, a lot of uncertainty remains \nregarding the weather for the weekend and start of next week.",
